{"title":"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_6_(A_Bit_slow.)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6 (A Bit slow.)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_🚀_Under_2_Min_🚀\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 🚀 Under 2 Min 🚀</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(easy_to_digest!)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to digest!)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An even number of circles are nested, starting with a radius of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and increasing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> each time, all sharing a common point. The region between every other circle is shaded, starting with the region inside the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> but outside the circle of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> An example showing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> circles is displayed below. What is the least number of circles needed to make the total shaded area at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/4/6843bb6f774ba13b9ca23e3cc319521d00357bb2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2023\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"49\" height=\"14\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/3/aa3c94ca7814105299a9086afbfcb5b4ecaf2609.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] filldraw(circle((0,0),8),gray); filldraw(circle((-1,0),7),white); filldraw(circle((-2,0),6),gray); filldraw(circle((-3,0),5),white); filldraw(circle((-4,0),4),gray); filldraw(circle((-5,0),3),white); filldraw(circle((-6,0),2),gray); filldraw(circle((-7,0),1),white); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/f/b7fbe0ebbbdc08e3eced13ef4855b78b666a9d1f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) } 46 \\qquad \\textbf{(B) } 48 \\qquad \\textbf{(C) } 56 \\qquad \\textbf{(D) } 60 \\qquad \\textbf{(E) } 64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"401\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Notice that the area of the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/b/03b24fc7d4c6ba2b5ef70cc708aa379d666ec266.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2^2\\pi-1^2\\pi)+(4^2\\pi-3^2\\pi)+(6^2\\pi-5^2\\pi)+ \\cdots + (n^2\\pi-(n-1)^2 \\pi)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"527\" height=\"21\" /> for any even number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>Using the difference of squares, this simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/1/6e12a32fb44f718b84fa556d8c3b66f0e2e9d9f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+2+3+4+\\cdots+n) \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"207\" height=\"20\" />. So, we are basically finding the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/c/bcc11febe3d378e2eb0a39b839e4ca3319705379.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{n(n+1)}{2}&gt;2023 \\Rightarrow n(n+1) &gt; 4046$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"290\" height=\"40\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875e240b060bfde110d878e46e9f385163f12ca5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60(61) &gt; 60^2=3600$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"21\" />, the only option higher than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~MrThinker\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After first observing the problem, we can work out a few of the areas.\n</p><p>1st area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56bbee03fcd961b5b9206fdf50f1c04c0080555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi-\\pi = 3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>2nd area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91b268304a9258f72d68526d16e261ba2c5ac11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\pi-9\\pi = 7\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>3rd area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0cbda26ebbbfbe5fd0a1a773459b52d54bc8fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36\\pi-25\\pi = 11\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>4th area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320e7fd9328afc970fef11b6ceaea727c3685511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\pi-49\\pi = 15\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>We can see that the pattern is an arithmetic sequence with first term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and common difference <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. From here, we can start from the bottom of the answer choices and work our way up. As the question asks for the least number of circles needed total, we have to divide the number of total circles by 2.\n</p><p>We can find the sum of the first <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/4/4f4b8590f8aa9f9894b3891dd5dede0e354fa04e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$32$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> terms of the arithmetic sequence by using the formula.\n</p><p>The last term is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/e/ece289e944f2bd7c006f4d67dd1084eb58111a54.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4\\cdot(32-1) = 127$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />. \n</p><p>Then, we can find the sum: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/8/6d854caaa58853344076e419b136f7ae0a252071.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3+127)/2 \\cdot 32 = 65\\cdot32 = 2080$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"20\" />. It is clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/e/05e228ac5bee7b9ffb60cacf50f3f2c7c31f8038.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"18\" height=\"13\" /> works.\n</p><p>The next answer choice is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, which we have to divide by 2 to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651ba418a810d971dbc8a326d49a71fe1541fae0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>The last term is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/7/767aa24d0cbd053a489102098f0e620783bad574.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 + 4\\cdot(30-1) = 119$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The sum is: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/4/db43c73500f2d04fed65fb09b0d4b23ffcb78073.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(3+119)/2 \\cdot 30 = 61\\cdot30 = 1830$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"258\" height=\"20\" />. This does not work.\n</p><p>As answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> does not work and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> does, we can conclude that the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~zgahzlkw\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Similar_to_Solution_2.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Similar_to_Solution_2)\">Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Similar to Solution 2)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can easily see that all of the answer choices are even, which helps us solve this problem a little.\n</p><p>Let's just not consider the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" />, since it is not that important, so let's cancel that out.\n</p><p>When we plug in 64, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/d/fdd4ae15767d754dd53aeb6f9560b1f0b04856f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64^2-63^2+62^2-61^2+\\cdots +4^2-3^2+2^2-1^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"369\" height=\"18\" />. By difference of squares, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/2/1229019085c72096bbbcf39f407b5fa5905c68ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1+2+3+\\cdots+62+63+64$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"238\" height=\"15\" />, which by the sum of an arithmetic sequence, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/e/89e5e6e61b5aee0600ccaa565e1642f84f464fe8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64(64+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"40\" />, which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/d/cbd42fdfe6f14b7a9bffe4194b3419ef6e19ee38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2080$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Similarly, we can use this for answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />, and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/4/3/a4393d572127e32af059b5f47e8eda7431debf2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{60(60+1)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"88\" height=\"40\" /> which is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/e/74e71ccf49f213e950c03a625608725261e661d5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1830$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>So, we see that answer choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is too small to satisfy the requirements, so we conclude the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~ESAOPS\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can consider making a table.\n</p><p>If there is 1 circle, the area of the shaded region is 0π. (We can write this as 0π.)\n</p><p>If there are 2 circles, the area of the shaded region is 3π.  (We can write this as (1+2)π).\n</p><p>If there are 3 circles, the area of the shaded region is 3π.  (We can write this as (1+2)π).\n</p><p>If there are 4 circles, the area of the shaded region is 10π.  (We can write this as (1+2+3+4)π).\n</p><p>If there are 5 circles, the area of the shaded region is 10π.  (We can write this as (1+2+3+4)π).\n</p><p>If there are 6 circles, the area of the shaded region is 21π.  (We can write this as (1+2+3+4+5+6)π).\n</p><p>Now the pattern emerges. When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even, the area of the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/8/ed80dbccf7db2f4bb9636734d7e39a7408fdcd1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(1+2+3+\\cdots+n)\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"175\" height=\"20\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/a/73a18b5569bea5403e399b7b1c2230e9bd16332a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left( \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\right) \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"113\" height=\"45\" />. But remember that the problem stated that there are an even number of circles. So now we are solving the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/c/24cbe15cb4d71ec0703cb4ae8ad5951916bbf834.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left( \\frac{n(n+1)}{2} \\right) \\pi\\ge2023\\pi.\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"43\" /> Dividing by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/c/f2ca003a7da0de4994b4733e203b74ff52d42553.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\pi$\" width=\"10\" height=\"8\" /> and multiplying by 2 on both sides, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5dcfbf236f4a3e1d29409b6f33ef0f0cdf01f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n(n+1)\\ge4046$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"130\" height=\"20\" />. Now we can plug in the answer choices, and we start off with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/2/302e99c1c7cd91a6ae371139e5142ccef5977dca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> because it is the only answer choice that is a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />. Plugging in we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/3/9/5396c095cdd47bf56f0c5ad96a0f38b3613f49e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$60\\cdot61=3660$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"112\" height=\"14\" />, and this is not quite yet more than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/c/2cc376309bd44024c2d6a263bc2ee550c8575824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4046$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"38\" height=\"14\" />. But only option <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/d/41dd6239c1c2a19d3d1debd91c269d68adeff3ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\text{E})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> is bigger, so we know that the solution can only be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php/User:Yrock\">Yrock</a>\n</p><p>(P.S. I did this in the test and I solved it in 2 minutes)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> the area of shaded region and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/c/10cb764f88509fb1c8012366993fdbee98f31bc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> the area of white region.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/c/4fc28e13617cbd31caeae965f561bec118e07910.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S &gt; W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/d/88da3e706cab3cb55149dd0a2c8be38353367f88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S \\approx W$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"58\" height=\"14\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is big.\nTherefore <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/f/f7f49084a12a5e4a3e979aa0d89120e7e2311b22.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\pi R^2 = S + W \\approx 2S \\ge 4046 \\pi \\implies R \\approx 64.\\]\" width=\"337\" height=\"18\" />\nSo we conclude the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p><b>vladimir.shelomovskii@gmail.com, vvsss</b>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_6_.28A_Bit_slow..29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6_(A_Bit_slow.)\">Solution 6 (A Bit slow.)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6 (A Bit slow.)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>After first observing the problem, we can work out a few of the areas.\n</p><p>1st area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/5/6/a56bbee03fcd961b5b9206fdf50f1c04c0080555.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\pi-\\pi = 3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>2nd area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/1/b91b268304a9258f72d68526d16e261ba2c5ac11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$16\\pi-9\\pi = 7\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"118\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>3rd area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/c/b0cbda26ebbbfbe5fd0a1a773459b52d54bc8fa2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36\\pi-25\\pi = 11\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>4th area = <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/0/320e7fd9328afc970fef11b6ceaea727c3685511.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$64\\pi-49\\pi = 15\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"136\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Notice that the area of the shaded region is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/933a7d2855d2ea8f869e8360c448f9ec0f0b9c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pi+7\\pi+11\\pi+15\\pi...+(4n-1)\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"281\" height=\"20\" /> for any even number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>We can create a formula to compute this sum by doing:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/3/933a7d2855d2ea8f869e8360c448f9ec0f0b9c13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3\\pi+7\\pi+11\\pi+15\\pi...+(4n-1)\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"281\" height=\"20\" />+<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/9/619d7ef251e0ce1792d8744ef043fd90e6f32521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4n-1)\\pi+...15\\pi+11\\pi+7\\pi+3\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"281\" height=\"20\" />\nto get\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/6/cc6aa607d8362e9b4f9ca9f487a746feddac6673.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(4n+2)*\\frac{n}{2} \\to (2n^2+n)\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"213\" height=\"34\" />\nIt is important to realize that each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> circles, the unshaded and the shaded.\nSo that means for each answer choice there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/c/2ec701493fa72dda5d6747fe14f30e7b1c2fb6c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> as many circles. \nThen we just plug in values (strategically) to get that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/5/e35e1cf0c2563c9bbe697e9a799e153f870c84e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2*(\\frac{64}{2})^2+(\\frac{64}{2})$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"130\" height=\"38\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/8/6b83402c2d47a7fe46f08b1f5c67df69b5d5a893.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(E) } 64}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" /> as the answer.\n</p><p>~algebraic_algorithmic\n</p><p>~kfclover (minor LaTeX edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Little_Fermat\">Video Solution by Little Fermat</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Little Fermat\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=TrswrE0Yt9UZW1uv&amp;t=3226\">https://youtu.be/h2Pf2hvF1wE?si=TrswrE0Yt9UZW1uv&amp;t=3226</a>\n~little-fermat\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_.28First_understand_the_problem.21.21.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Math-X_(First_understand_the_problem!!!)\">Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Math-X (First understand the problem!!!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=-FmeM--j5ohBx4eR&amp;t=3784\">https://youtu.be/GP-DYudh5qU?si=-FmeM--j5ohBx4eR&amp;t=3784</a>\n</p><p>~Math-X\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_.F0.9F.9A.80_Under_2_Min_.F0.9F.9A.80\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_🚀_Under_2_Min_🚀\">Video Solution 🚀 Under 2 Min 🚀</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 🚀 Under 2 Min 🚀\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/QBpDSj-Ew_4\">https://youtu.be/QBpDSj-Ew_4</a>\n</p><p><i> ~Education, the Study of Everything </i>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_.28easy_to_digest.21.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Power_Solve_(easy_to_digest!)\">Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to digest!)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Power Solve (easy to digest!)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/m1a4xgjZLmc\">https://youtu.be/m1a4xgjZLmc</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_.5B.F0.9F.94.A5Fast_and_Easy.F0.9F.94.A5.5D\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_CosineMethod_[🔥Fast_and_Easy🔥]\">Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by CosineMethod [🔥Fast and Easy🔥]\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qjI3FuhS3IQ\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qjI3FuhS3IQ</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_SpreadTheMathLove\">Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by SpreadTheMathLove\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BaDXj32nFXY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=BaDXj32nFXY</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/rZrsrMxA7v0\">https://youtu.be/rZrsrMxA7v0</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A\">2023 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 14\">Problem 14</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 16\">Problem 16</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_1\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2023 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2023_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_3\"